+        "file": "infrastructure/modules/sql.bicep",
+        "line": 11,
+        "what": "Pipeline runs CREATE USER ... FROM EXTERNAL PROVIDER as a service principal, but the SQL server has no identity with Graph/Directory Readers rights, so the grant step fails",
+        "why": "This acceptance line needs the app's managed identity to reach Entra-only SQL. The pipeline signs in as the service-connection principal (stage-template.yml line 90) and runs CREATE USER [$(appName)] FROM EXTERNAL PROVIDER. When a service principal runs that statement, Azure SQL looks up the name in Microsoft Graph using the logical server's own identity. That identity needs User.Read.All, GroupMember.Read.All and Application.Read.All, or the Directory Readers role. sql.bicep gives the server no identity block, and neither the template nor its comments name the prerequisite. As written, the first deploy to any environment fails at the 'Grant the app's managed identity database access' step, and the app's identity never gets a database user. checker and bicep build only test the text, so neither can catch this. David must be able to defend this line, and an Azure reviewer will ask about this exact step.",
