+        "rule_id": "F5-acceptance: idempotent migrations",
+        "severity": "P2",
+        "file": "infrastructure/pipelines/azure-pipelines.yml",
+        "line": 38,
+        "what": "dotnet-ef is installed globally with no version, so the migration script's tool version depends on the day the pipeline runs",
+        "why": "This is the dotnet-ef pinning carry-over (9.0.9 vs runtime 10.0.13), which every snapshot from F0b to F4 assigned to F5 (docs/qa/build-F0b.md step 18 note). The pipeline now repeats the problem: the version of the idempotent script's generator is not reproducible, and it can drift from EF Core 10.0.13 in Directory.Packages.props. pre-push uses `dotnet tool restore`, but the repo has no tool manifest.",
